Constraint and grading code
---------------------------

  IFEvalG verifiers, Allen Institute for AI (open-instruct), from Google
  Research's instruction_following_eval. Apache License 2.0. Vendored in
  reliquary_general/_ifeval/ (same bytes as reliquary-instruction-following's
  copy). The verifiable-instruction prompts are WildChat prompts with
  constraints drawn from these verifiers' own templates.

  The structured-output grading rule restates NVIDIA NeMo Gym's
  structured_outputs resource server (https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Gym,
  commit 016bb6b811aa3cf27217d3385e981771115f7b88, Apache License 2.0) on the
  standard library; no NeMo Gym code is copied.

Changes made to every source: English prompts kept; prompts with e-mail
addresses or phone numbers dropped; a short lexicon of extreme content dropped
outside the safety block; exact and near (MinHash, Jaccard >= 0.7 on word
5-grams) duplicates removed within and across sources, including against the
prompts of reliquary-instruction-following; prompts sharing 8-grams with
IFEval, IFBench, Arena-Hard v2, MT-Bench, BFCL v4, tau2-bench, When2Call,
XSTest, MMLU-Pro or GPQA Diamond removed; rows whose tools carry a function
name from tau2-bench removed, and for xLAM also from BFCL v4 and When2Call; rows sampled, reformatted into chat
messages and reordered.
